{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/378018-embed-or-exploit","id":378018,"title":"Embed or Exploit?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-22T07:28:46-08:00","id":378018,"title":"Embed or Exploit?","content":"The Exploit Ultimatum from <i>Flowers of Hell</i> is interesting. It got me thinking of a converse power a demon might employ, a carrot to Ultimatum's stick: do this and you will be rewarded. The way I see it, the demon gives the human a task, if the human completes it, they gain a positive Condition of the demon's choosing (Inspired, Steadfast, Paid Handsomely, etc). It's the sort of power an Unchained might use on their cultists, or to entice a mortal into signing a Pact later on down the line (though the power probably explicitly counts as &quot;supernatural compulsion&quot; with regards to Pact-making).<br /> <br /> Anyway, do you guys think this sounds more like an Embed or an Exploit? It's definitely more subtle than Ultimatum, and it's less direct control than, say, The Word. Then again, Affliction is an Exploit that causes Conditions, so I could see it going either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T13:05:14-08:00","id":378310,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Perhaps an Exploit version would look something like so:<br /> <br /> <b>Just Rewards</b><br /> <br /> For some, the carrot is a much greater motivator than the stick. When payday is all that matters, a demon can utilize this Exploit to get reluctant mortals to do their bidding. When an Unchained activates this Exploit on a mortal, choose a task for them to carry out, as well as either a Condition to grant, or one to resolve. A demon could reward a mortal with Connections, for instance, or by removing an Addiction. The Condition granted or removed does not have to be necessarily a net boon for the mortal involved; you might promise to take care of a human's heroin addiction by drugging her up. Sometimes this is part of a convoluted scheme to throw off God-Machine agents. Other times it's just because demons can be mean fuckers when they want to.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Prerequisites:</b> Animal Messenger, You Can Trust Me<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Persuasion + Primum<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The reward doesn't come. If the mortal carries out the task successfully anyway, the demon gains the Leveraged Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> Nothing happens, either way.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> If the mortal carries out the command successfully within (successes + Primum) days, he receives the promised reward. Conditions gain this way are resolved as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The tasked mortal feels invigorated while working for the demon, gaining +2 to any rolls undertaken in pursuit of the task.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T02:55:07-08:00","id":378863,"title":"","content":"sounds like a conditional pact","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T20:36:13-08:00","id":383934,"title":"","content":"I think an Embed for movie style hacking would be cool <br /> <br /> Digital Pwng<br /> <br /> Most people rarely know how a computer works and it seems like digital magic to them. Using this a demon can use there computer hacking skills to hack into systems that they should not be able to access such as cars, houses and many other systems that a computer should not be able to interface with. This embed also makes the users computer screen look dam awesome when they start there hacking. Once they have control of the system they can do things such as causing the system to explode and other things you have seen in the movies. <br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Computers + The system being used<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: When the user start to hack into the system they trip the systems digital secure measures even from systems that should not have them. There current location is given to the enemy. As well as the system may blow up in there face causing system rank Lethal Damage.<br /> <br /> Failure: You Fail to get into the system and system admins have been alerted. <br /> <br /> Success: You have Gained root access to the system and can now do as you will with the system. If you blow up the system Hit + System Rating = Lethal damage for the explosion. <br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: Still thinking this one over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T23:23:32-08:00","id":384013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/378018-embed-or-exploit?p=383934#post383934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think an Embed for movie style hacking would be cool</div> </div> </div> </div>You appear to have preemptively made this an Exploit, if the flashy visuals and the dicepool with a Power Attribute in it are any indication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T03:53:06-08:00","id":384076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/378018-embed-or-exploit?p=384013#post384013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You appear to have preemptively made this an Exploit, if the flashy visuals and the dicepool with a Power Attribute in it are any indication.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmm so how would you change it to make it fit into a embed better then ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T09:40:50-08:00","id":384292,"title":"","content":"Remove the dice-pool and make it subtle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T11:33:33-08:00","id":387511,"title":"","content":"better ??<br /> <br /> Digital Pwng<br /> <br /> Most people rarely know how a computer works and it seems like digital magic to them. Using this a demon can use their computer hacking skills to hack into systems that they should not be able to access such as cars, houses and many other systems that a computer should not be able to interface with. This embed also makes the user's computer screen look dam awesome when they start there hacking. Once they have control of the system they can do things such as causing the system to explode and other things you have seen in the movies. <br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Computers + The system being used<br /> <br /> <br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> <br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: When the user start to hack into the system they trip the systems digital secure measures even from systems that should not have them. Their current location is given to the enemy. As well as the system may blow up in their face causing system rank Lethal Damage.<br /> <br /> Failure: You Fail to get into the system and system admins have been alerted. <br /> <br /> Success: You have Gained root access to the system and can now do as you will with the system even if the system should not have the ability to do something such ask hacking into network and controlling the power in the building.<br /> <br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: You can cause a system to overload If you blow up the system Hit + System Rating = Lethal damage for the explosion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T09:25:32-08:00","id":388493,"title":"","content":"That still sounds kind of exploit-y. <br /> <br /> Embeds, by nature, are subtle magic. Plausible things, something that could conceivably happen in reality. Coincidental. <br /> <br /> The fact that you want to pull off something, like out of hackers, with just the screen alone is a hint that you want it to be &quot;flashy.&quot; Vulgar, to use the mage term. That's very much what Exploits are. You know what else causes changes to the target of your powers? Exploits like hellfire (warps the gun you use), Hellhound (warps the animal). And so on.<br /> <br /> Take a look at the Cacaphony embeds. The three closest to what you want are <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Combustion, Shatter, and Sabotage. Combustion makes it more likely to catch flame. Sabotage makes a system shut down due to faulty equipment. Shatter is something you break with a physical strike, as if the materials were stressed. What you want is more powerful than all three.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, it could work as an interlock, just because we have no strong guidelines on what or what isn't a good interlock is, other than they're neither Embeds, nor Exploits, so can use whatever you want.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, that's what I always tell my Demon players. Want a custom rule/power/ etc? Congrats, we just decided on your next Interlock. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}